From 371390ceaa2ea238b2697ac9eb91f30bed0b6639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:37:54 -0400
Subject: Let "File removed" recover when the file comes back, and make Reload
 work

Omawrite 0.5.0 decides `deleted` once, at the instant QFileSystemWatcher
fires (backend.cpp: `!QFileInfo::exists(path)`), and never looks again.
Editors and agents that rewrite a file by unlink-then-create trip this:
the handler runs in the gap, the dialog says "File removed", and the file
is back on disk before the user reads it. The watch on the old inode is
gone, so nothing ever corrects the dialog.

ExternalChangeDialog.qml then sets `enabled: !root.deleted` on Reload, but
SquareDialogButton.qml overrides background/contentItem without consulting
`enabled`, so the disabled button is painted exactly like an enabled one.
Net effect: a bright blue Reload that swallows clicks.

Fix:
 - backend: after reporting a removal, watch the parent directory. When the
   file reappears, re-arm the file watch and emit externalChangeDetected
   (false, ...) if the contents differ, or a new externalFileRestored() if
   they are byte-identical.
 - backend: reloadFromDisk() re-checks the disk; if the file is still gone
   it falls back to keepExternalVersion() with a status line, so the button
   is never a dead click.
 - dialog: Reload stays enabled in the removed state.
 - Main.qml: externalFileRestored closes a stale "File removed" dialog.
 - SquareDialogButton: paint a disabled state (opacity) so any future
   disabled button actually looks disabled.
 - tests: reportsRemovedFileComingBack, reloadOfMissingFileKeepsText.

Upstream: https://github.com/omacom-io/omawrite (issue drafted locally in
~/pkgs/omawrite/upstream-issue-stale-file-removed.md).
Retires when upstream includes this change (or an equivalent) in 0.5.1+.

